      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Ethernere Tainted West Karana [zone=939]\n**Who:**\n- Commander Galenth [npc=44037]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Cloak of the Doomscale Ritualist [item=113375]\n- Flaming Pumpkin Piece [item=113397]\n- Jack Bomb [item=113453]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Furball Miller [npc=44265]\n- Guard Sorkins [npc=44319]\n- Guard Wagsley [npc=44038]\n- Henina Miller [npc=44331]\n- Ritualist Danin [npc=44353]\n- a Doomscale resurrectionist [npc=44143]\n- a burning scarecrow [npc=44122]\n- a crispy jack [npc=44128]\n- a cultist`s barrel [npc=44130]\n- a cultist`s box [npc=44131]\n- a flaming jack [npc=44147]\n- a smoldering scarecrow [npc=44207]\n- an insane scarecrow [npc=44246]\n- an unstable spirit [npc=44254]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Ethernere #1: Overcoming the Cataclysm [quest=7249]\n- Ethernere #3: Answering the Call [quest=7251]\n- Raid Expedition: The Doomscale Horde [quest=7253]\n- The Doomscale Horde [quest=7252]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Oct 8 05:11:37 2013\nModified: Thu Dec 12 03:17:16 2024 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task is the second in a series of three. It begins with Commander Galenth ( **click for map image**) in the Ethernere Tainted West Karana. He is located in the northeastern part of the zone._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 95\n\\- Completed \"Overcoming the Cataclysm\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Galenth'\nCommander Galenth says 'Are you a slayer of dragons? Don't lie to me! Your fancy dress tells the truth better than your mouth! We have problems here, problems bigger than burnt homes and stranded settlers: problems with bigger teeth. No, I heard of your work, how you coddle the civs. You'd be more fit as a [worshiper] of dragons than a slayer of them!'\nYou say, 'A worshiper?'\nCommander Galenth says 'You disagree? I mark you unfairly? Twenty years in the guard, and you learn how to judge a man. You learn that most are weak, that they'll sell themselves to anything that gives them a warm bed, warm soup, and a mind free of worries and thoughts. You learn that fancy folks in fancy dress are [followers], not fighters!'\nYou say, 'Followers?'\nCommander Galenth says 'And that's why I'll use you. You're gonna follow me, and you're gonna convince those cultists you follow the dragon. You can follow [instructions], too, can't you?'\nYou say, 'Instructions?'\nCommander Galenth says 'Your dress isn't fancy enough, and those dragon lovers aren't gonna embrace you and seat you at the right claw of their scaly god the first time you bend a knee! Thievery is in order. Either you [help] and show you're worth something, or I'll find another silk-pantalooned dandy to do the deed!'\nYou say, 'I suppose I'll help...'\nCommander Galenth says 'Good. You're gonna steal one of their fancy cloaks from their supply crates or barrels, and then you'll listen in on the resurrectionist ceremonies. I need to know what these dragon lovers are planning!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Not of This World'.\nCommander Galenth has asked you to learn more about the Doomscale cultists and their connection to the dragon.\n\n---\n\nFind a ritualist robe in one of the cultists' barrels or crates 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ You need to find a robe to disguise yourself as a cultist. You can probably find one in barrels or crates owned by the cultists. But be careful they aren't around to see you stealing their goods!\n_Loot a \"Cloak of the Doomscale Ritualist\" from one of the barrels or crates (does not always drop) in the northeastern part of the zone ( **click for map image** \\-\\- just south of the portal area and Lady Lendiniara). Note that the Doomscale NPCs in the area may attack you when you do this._\n\n---\n\nGet close to the resurrectionists and listen to them while wearing the robe you stole 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Wearing the robe, get near the resurrectionists and listen to their chants.\n_This update is around /location -1115, -4150, -471. Stand in the middle of the resurrectionist circle and click the robe for the update._\nWearing the cultist robe, you pass as one of them and hear them chanting, 'Powers beyond Norrath, shrouded creatures beyond the veil of death, hear us! Release unto us the souls of the once-living. Return to this world the ones who wait in the gray that they might guide us into realms beyond, realms revealed by the Dragon of Doom!' You see the souls of dead appearing and disappearing from the vents connected to otherworldly places.\nan unstable spirit appears out of the mist.\nan unstable spirit decoheres and returns to the mist.\nan unstable spirit dissipates.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Commander Galenth 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Tell Commander Galenth what you have discovered.\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Galenth'\nCommander Galenth says 'My fancy chum, back once more! What a fine follower you make! A place beyond the grave? So the dragon comes from a land of the dead...monstrous! The sooner we strike, the sooner we save these lands! But the troops aren't going anywhere until we secure more knowledge about the dragon and its lovers. Sorkins went southwest to the farms to follow the cult, but he hasn't reported back. Find that dog and make sure he hasn't deserted, and collect what knowledge you can!'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Guard Sorkins 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ The cultists also have plans for the southern regions of West Karana. Find Guard Sorkins and get his report on what's happening.\n_Guard Sorkins and Henina Miller are found in the far south-central boundary of the zone ( **click for map image**)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Guard Sorkins'\nGuard Sorkins says 'I know, I know: Galenth waits on my report! I followed a group of cultists and overheard them talking about sacrificing souls in order to gain more power in the other world. But I can't just leave now! Henina will tear my arm out of the socket! Apparently her boys have disappeared, and one was taken by the group of cultists. See if you can calm her down!'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Henina Miller 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Cultists have kidnapped Henina's son. Ask her what happened.\nYou say, 'Hail, Henina Miller'\nHenina Miller says 'Thank goodness you're here! This Sorkins fellow is worthless! I've told him a dozen times to go get [Furball] back, but he just makes excuses about needing to brief his commander! He's nothing better than a coward! I told him about my plan to use the scarecrows to make a bomb, but not even that would give him courage!'\nYou say, 'Furball?'\nHenina Miller says 'Yes, my son! Well, he's my adopted son, but I love him just as much as Cleet Jr. or Tiny! A group of cloaked villains passed through the flames and grabbed Furball while we were searching for some of our lost belongings. If only the rest of the [family] were here, we'd get the job done ourselves!'\nYou say, 'Where is your family?'\nHenina Miller says 'Cleet and Tiny set off to Qeynos to get help a few days ago, and I haven't seen them since. I hope they're okay! Cleet Jr. and Furball stayed here to protect the farm, but Cleet Jr. just couldn't sit still. He's wandered off to find the find the Qeynos guard and join them. That boy just thinks about fighting all day and never listens! A fat lot of good the Qeynos guard has been doing anyway! We really need your help, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! If you can bring me some pumpkin pieces from those flaming jacks, I know a little secret [recipe] that will make this easier.'\nYou say, 'What about that recipe?'\nHenina Miller says 'Well, I did say it's a secret, but I know that if you bake some pieces of flaming wisp lightstones into a pie, those cultists will be in for a treat! Go to it, please! Bring me those pumpkin pieces, and save Furball!'\n\n---\n\nCollect Flaming Pumpkin Pieces from the flaming jacks 0/7 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Henina Miller wants you to rescue her son, Furball, and she has a plan. She has asked you to collect Flaming Pumpkin Pieces from the flaming jacks so that she can bake them into an explosive pie.\n_In the south-central part of the zone, find and kill scarecrow mobs until you've looted seven items. These are average mobs, hitting for a max ~13,000 (mezzable; stunnable)._\nDeliver 7 Flaming Pumpkin Piece to Henina Miller 0/7 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Give the Flaming Pumpkin Pieces to Henina Miller so she can make the pie.\nHenina Miller says 'That's everything I need! You're so kind and helpful! You know, it almost feels like I've met you before, but my memory isn't as good as it used to be. Anyway, I cooked this up nice and fresh in those coals over there. It'll give those cultists a real kick!'\n_You receive a \"Jack Bomb\"._\n\n---\n\nThrow the Jack Bomb at Ritualist Danin and his followers 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Find Furball Miller and throw the Jack Bomb on Ritualist Danin and his followers.\n_Get close to Ritualist Danin ( **click for map image**), target him, right-click the Jack Bomb, then left-click anywhere within the Ritualist's general area:_\na Doomscale ritualist outstretches his hand towards the Dragon.\nRitualist Danin falls to the ground, scorched by the exploding pumpkin. As his life fades, his voice rasps, 'Now my brethren and I shall be the sacrifice! We travel to the gray, the space unseen by gods and mortals. We make way for all who follow, for all of Norrath that shall be swallowed! The dragon will claim her brood and secure them in the gray for all eternity.'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Furball Miller 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Tell Furball Miller that he is safe.\n_Furball Miller ( **click for map image**) is found at the bottom of the lava fall in the central part of the zone._\nYou say, 'Hail, Furball Miller'\nFurball Miller says 'BARK! Thank you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! I thought I was going to be skinned, cooked in lava, and eaten! They kept talking about bleeding this world and offering its life to the dragon. Our blood would secure their place in the world between worlds. It's crazy, bark! Is mother alright? She must be worried! I can get back from here, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I'm worried about Cleet Jr., though! He went southwest, chasing after cultists and following some guard name Wagsley, trying to find adventure. He's not cut out for that, bark! Go find him!'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Guard Wagsley 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Cleet Miller, Jr. wants to join the Qeynos Guard and has run after a guard named Wagsley. Find Wagsley and discover where Cleet, Jr. has gone.\n_Guard Wagsley ( **click for map image**) is found in the southwestern part of the zone._\nYou say, 'Hail, Guard Wagsley'\nGuard Wagsley says 'Cleet Miller, Jr.? Yeah, I've heard of him. He's that stupid boy right over there! Got himself run up the tree by those glowing ghastlies! I would just hoof it back to camp, but I kind of feel bad leaving a kid behind who's been crying for his mommy for over an hour. But look at the size of those creatures! I'm not going anywhere near 'em! What, are you going to do something?'\nYou have discovered that the Doomscale cultists are trying to lower the barrier between the world of Norrath and the threshold of the afterlife. In the process, you saved Furball Miller from being sacrificed. However, Cleet Miller, Jr. is still in quite a predicament.\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nExperience",
