6041]\n- a widowling [npc=46042]\n- an injured villager [npc=46055]\n- an offended sapling [npc=46043]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Daily Task: Heroic Adventures [quest=7988]\n- Estle #2: Remember the Dead [quest=7406]\n- Estle #3: The Other Brother [quest=7407]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Jan 22 03:53:15 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Brother Estle ( **click for map image**) in the Ethernere Tainted West Karana. He is located in the northwestern part of the zone, just southwest of the floating village (/location 265, -280, -91)._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 75\n\\- No tasks\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"help\" to request the task and \"go\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\n\\- Speak with Brother Estle 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update.\n\\-\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update.\n\n---\n\n**Step #2:**\n\\-\nDestroy the rubble piles and widows that have trapped the villagers in their homes 0/37\n\\-\\-\\- These are the \"a rubble \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\" destructible objects around the village.\n\\-\nCreate a healing poultice and use it to cure the injured villagers 0/8\n\\-\\-\\- Loot quest items (three of each) from bears and saplings in the area, give them to Brother Estle, then right-click the returned item on injured villagers.\n\n---\n\n**Step #3:**\n\\-\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update (receive \"Brother Estle's Prayer Book\").\n\\-\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update (receive \"Grave Shovel\" and \"Corpse Rope\").\n\\-\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update (no item given)\n\n---\n\n**Step #4:**\n\\-\nRead Estle's prayer over the dead villagers 0/11\n\\-\\-\\- Target \"a dead villager\" and right-click the Prayer Book to spawn \"a departing spirit\"; kill the spirit.\n\\-\nDig graves, drag the deomposing villagers to the graves, and bury them 0/11\n\\-\\-\\- Around /location 200, 0, -97, right-click the \"Grave Shovel\" to spawn a grave; then go to \"a decomposing village\" and right-click \"Corpse Rope\" on it; lead them to the spawned grave. You can drag multiple corpses at the same time. (Mobs attack as you lead the villagers away).\n\\-\nKill the fire spirits and use their essences near the piles of rotting villagers so that the corpses ignite 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Loot \"Fire Spirit Essence\" from \"a fire spirit\"; target \"a rotting villager\" and right-click essence on them.\n\n---\n\n**Step #5:**\n\\-\nSpeak with a spirit crier 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update.\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n\n---\n\n**Step #6:**\n\\-\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update.\n\n---\n\n**Step #7:**\n\\-\nKill the raiders that are attacking the villagers 0/7\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the gehein raiders.\n\\-\nSearch for the villagers that ran into the Ethernere tunnels, and kill any resistance you meet 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- Kill updates (tunnel entrance by /loc 445, -600, -82: soul consumers and soul feasters).\n\\-\nRecover axes from the thieves and arm the villagers so they can defend themselves 0/8\n\\-\\-\\- Loot 8x \"Sturdy Defensive Axe\" from \"a weapon thief\", then give the axes to villagers in the floating house (/loc 315, -440, 52).\n\n---\n\n**Step #8:**\n\\-\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update (no item received).\n\\-\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update (receive \"Magical Trap\").\n\\-\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update (no item received).\n\n---\n\n**Step #9:**\n\\-\nKill the eradicators when Estle weakens them 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- Kill updates: gehein eradicators, skirth eradicators, tirun eradicators.\n\\-\nTrap the soul slurpers with Estle's trap and then kill them before they can reach the villagers 0/7\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the \"a soul slurper\" mobs that spawn and walks up the spiral ramp; \"Magical Trap\" can be used to spawn an aura that will freeze these mobs in place (40 seconds).\n\\-\nKill Brutallion to prevent it from completely destroying the village 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill \"Brutallion\", who spawns and starts destroying houses.\n\n---\n\n**Step #10:**\n\\-\nSpeak with a spiritual emissary 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update.\n\n---\n\n**Step #11:**\n\\-\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update.\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #11 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**MAP**\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_\"a vengeful spirit\" (or its PH) has a chance to spawn after the fifth step is completed. Known loot from this named:_\nLevel 100\nSpiritist's Ornate Aegis\nSplinter of Potency\nLevel 95\n???\nLevel 90\n???\nLevel 85\n???\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n**TRIGGERING THE TASK**\nYou say, 'Hail, Brother Estle'\nBrother Estle shakes his head as he surveys the devastation. 'When I first came to minister to the people of West Karana, I never thought this would be their fate. I imagined I would carry the message of the Prime Healer to all the people and bring peace to their souls. I imagined these lands would prosper and that my brothers and I would establish a new temple that would be the spiritual foundation of the Karanas. But when the light of [reality] shines, imagination often withers like shadows in the noonday sun .'\nYou say, 'Reality?'\nBrother Estle says 'Who can say what shadow plays of imagination will foretell the future? The first act in my mind's theatre never showed to me the betrayal by my brother, Trintle. His spirit having been fouled by the cult of Bertoxxulous in the sewers below Qeynos, he attacked me one night on the road. Were it not for the help of a passing adventurer much like you, my body would have been as broken as these lands are now. Instead, Trintle went to his grave, and Chintle and I thought long about whether to abandon our mission and return to the temple. We decided the souls of the people were more important than our anguish at the loss of our brother. We thought our [vision] was still possible.'\nYou say, 'What vision?'\nBrother Estle says 'Now I can see how naive it was. The play has become a tragedy.' Brother Estle sighs. 'The old visions are unwelcome. I can think of nothing lofty. What is left to me now is worry and duty. As a healer, I must attend to the injured. If I lose their bodies, I will also lose their souls. If only [Brother Chintle] we're here to aid me in such an impossible task.'\nYou say, 'Brother Chintle?'\nBrother Estle says 'He was always even more naive than I. He could never accept that Brother Trintle's evil was not some sort of possession or mind control, just as he could not accept that such an enormous calamity could fall upon West Karana apart from the wrath of some evil spirit or god. Shortly after the tragedy occurred, Chintle began speaking of visions -- visions of Brother Trintle and the truth behind what happened here. He ran off in the night, and I have not seen him since. I fear for his safety and sanity, but now my [task] has doubled in difficulty without him. I cannot search for him when there is so much suffering with which I must contend.'\nYou say, 'What task?'\nBrother Estle says 'There are injured who need healing, dead that lie unburied, and hungry who need food. The tasks are more than enough for one man, and the Qeynos guard are already stretched thin. You have seen the plight of the people. Will you [help], adventurer? If we can tend to the needs of the people, perhaps then I can search for Chintle and heal his troubled mind.'\nYou say, 'I will help!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Life After Death'.\nBrother Estle needs your help: The village has been destroyed and people are dead or gravely injured. He has asked you to help him restore order to the village, since his fellow mercenary, Brother Chintle, has gone missing.\nBrother Estle says 'Thank you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. [Go] and prepare. Speak to me when you are ready.'\n**STEP #1**\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak with Brother Estle to find out how you can help the villagers.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail update. His response depends on the next step._\n_If you get rubble piles next:_\nBrother Estle says 'When the earthquakes shook the village, homes collapsed. Many people were trapped in the rubble. We tried to free them, but widow spiders, displaced by the quakes, have infested the destroyed homes. I am sure it will not be long before those left alive will be consumed by the spiders. Help the trapped villagers if you can. Clear the rubble and kill the widows.'\n_If you get injured villagers next:_\nResponse?\n\n---\n\n**STEP #2**\nDestroy the rubble piles and widows that have trapped the villagers in their homes 0/37 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ When the earthquakes came, many villagers were trapped in their homes when they collapsed. Now widows have taken residence in the rubble and threaten the lives of the villagers. Destroy the rubble piles and kill the widows to free the trapped villagers.\n_If You Get This Step: These are the \"a rubble pile\" and \"a rubble widow\" destructible objects around the village. The widows are fairly simple mobs, and the rubble piles don't have too many hitpoints. Some of the piles will spawn trivial mobs called \"a widowling\"._\n=====================\nCreate a healing poultice and use it to cure the injured villagers 0/8 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says: Brother Estle needs your help to concoct a poultice that can heal the injured villagers. He nees you to : Collect 3 Bear Bile samples from bilious bears. Collect 3 Sapling Resin samples from offended saplings. Collect 3 Saplings Charcoal samples from burnt saplings. Give the samples to Brother Estle, and he will make the poultice. You can then heal the injured villagers using the poultice._\n_If You Get This Step: Kill bilious bears, offended saplings, and burnt saplings until you've looted 3x \"Bear Bile\", 3x \"Sapling Resin, and 3x \"Sapling Charcoal\" (respectively). Hand in these items to Brother Estle to receive \"Brother Estle's Poultice\", then right-click this item on \"an injured villager\" mobs._\n\n---\n\n**STEP #3**\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak with Brother Estle to find out what else he needs you to do.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail update (receive \"Brother Estle's Prayer Book\")._\n=====================\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak with Brother Estle to find out what else he needs you to do.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail update (receive \"Grave Shovel\" and \"Corpse Rope\")._\n=====================\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak with Brother Estle to find out what else he needs you to do.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail update (no item given)._\nBrother Estle says 'The miasma of death is overpowering. So many have died that it will take ages to bury them all. It pains me to think that we cannot pay the proper respect to the dead, but the living will surely join them if we do not do what is necessary. We need the hottest fires. Burning spirits have been flitting around the village, no doubt loosed from the depths of the earth by the quakes. Kill them, take their essences, and use them to kindle the piles of corpses.'\n\n---\n\n**STEP #4**\nRead Estle's prayer over the dead villagers 0/11 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says: Brother Estle wants to give safe travel to the souls of the recently departed villagers. Use his prayer book over the dead villagers to speak his words to the lingering souls._\n_If You Get This Step: Target \"a dead villager\" and right-click the Prayer Book to spawn \"a departing spirit\"; kill the spirit._\n=====================\nDig graves, drag the decomposing villagers to the graves, and bury them 0/11 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n**Task Window**: Decomposing corpses are starting to stink up the village. Brother Estle wants you to give them a proper burial. To do so, he has given you a Grave Shovel and a Corpse Rope. Use the Grave Shovel in the open area to the west of the village, past the last houses, to dig graves. Use the Corpse Rope on the decomposing villagers to drag them to the graves. If a decomposing villager touches a grave, they will be buries automatically.\n_If You Get This Step: Around /location 200, 0, -97, right-click the \"Grave Shovel\" to spawn a grave; then go to \"a decomposing villager\" and right-click \"Corpse Rope\" on it; lead them to the spawned grave. Mobs will attack as you lead the villagers away. Make sure you take off any form of levitation for this part._\n=====================\nKill the fire spirits and use their essences near the piles of rotting villagers so that the corpses ignite 0/5 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ There are so many piles of rotting corpses in the village that the stench has become overwhelming. Brother Estle wants you to burn the piles. To kindle a proper flame, you will need to kill fire spirits, take their Fire Spirit Essences, and use them on the piles of rotting villagers.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill mephits called \"a fire spirit\", located northeast of the floating village. Loot the essences from their corpses, and use them on the groups of rotting villagers around the area._\n\n---\n\n**STEP #5**\nSpeak with a spirit crier 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ A mysterious spirit has appeared, calling out to all the villagers. Speak with the spirit crier and see what it wants.\n_If You Get This Step: The spirit caller can be found roaming beneath the floating house._\na spirit crier shouts 'Members of the living, take heed! Listen to my words! The Horde is coming! The Brother shall lead them here! You will join our ranks!'\na spirit crier shouts 'Your place is among the dead, and the Horde will be your masters!'\na spirit crier shouts 'The Brother has spoken: The Karanas are damned! Lay down your lives to us and prepare for your inevitable servitude!'\n_Hail it:_\nYou say, 'Hail, a spirit crier'\na spirit crier says 'You are wise to stand before me, yes. You are wise to yield. Soon we come. Soon the living will become the dead!'\n\n---\n\n**STEP #6**\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Talk to Brother Estle about what the spirit said and what is in store for the village.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail update._\nBrother Estle says 'So the spirit speaks of the glowing creatures that have harried this village since the disaster? They must be planning an assault, but I cannot say what the spirit meant by 'Brother.' I could not think that Chintle would be in collusion with them...' Brother Estle cups his hands around his mouth and yells, 'Everyone, retreat to the floating house! The Horde is coming, and we have no chance on the ground!' Brother Estle watches as people run about, panicked. He sees a group dashing into the underground tunnels. 'No! I have seen creatures of the Horde emerge from there! Surely they will be lost if they enter the realm below! Go after them. Hopefully nothing ill befalls them, but if the worst happens, pay back the Horde in kind!'\n\n---\n\n**STEP #7**\nKill the raiders that are attacking the villagers 0/7 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n**Task Window**: The villagers have retreated to the floating house, but this is not enough. Brother Estle wants to arm them in case the Horde finds them there. Brother Estle has asked you to kill the weapon thieves that have taken over the destroyed weapon shop, retrieve the Sturdy Defensive Axes, and give them to the villagers.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill the gehein raiders._\n=====================\nSearch for the villagers that ran into the Ethernere tunnels, and kill any resistance you meet 0/10 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Brother Estle has called for the villagers to retreat into the floating house, but a group of villagers were disoriented with fright and ran into the underground tunnels. You must search for the villagers in the tunnels and kill anything that might prey upon them.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill updates (tunnel entrance by /loc 445, -600, -82: soul consumers and soul feasters)._\n=====================\nRecover axes from the thieves and arm the villagers so they can defend themselves 0/8 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Loot 8x \"Sturdy Defensive Axe\" from \"a weapon thief\", then give the axes to villagers in the floating house (/loc 315, -440, 52)._\n\n---\n\n**STEP #8**\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak with Brother Estle and prepare for the oncoming Horde.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail update (no item received - leads into the first option in Step #9)._\nBrother Estle says 'Here they come from the tunnels in the village and the outskirts in the east! They shall attack the floating house; I am sure of it. The Horde will soon be upon us, but as they ascend the ramp, I shall do what I can to weaken them with my magic. Kill them before they can assault the villagers!'\n=====================\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak with Brother Estle and prepare for the oncoming Horde.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail update (receive \"Magical Trap\" - leads into the second option in Step #9)._\n=====================\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak with Brother Estle and prepare for the oncoming Horde.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail update (no item received - leads into the third option in Step #9)._\n\n---\n\n**STEP #9**\nKill the eradicators when Estle weakens them 0/10 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Kill the eradicators as they climb the ramp to the floating house. They come from the tunnels in the village and the eastern outskirts. Brother Estle will weaken them when they are close to him.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill updates: gehein eradicators, skirth eradicators, tirun eradicators. These are staggered spawns that make their way towards Brother Estle's location. Once in range of him, he weakens them to 30% health. They hit for a max ~12,000 and summon when damaged, so don't take them too lightly. Note you can kill them without bringing them to Brother Estle, but will just have to do so from 100% health._\n=====================\nTrap the soul slurpers with Estle's trap and then kill them before they can reach the villagers 0/7 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n**Task Window**: The soul slurpers are coming from the tunnels in the village or the eastern outskirts. They seek the villagers hiding in the floating house. Use the Magical Trap to freeze the soul slurpers in place for a short while, and then kill them.\n\"Sippin suggests below to put your group at the top of the transparent ramp. When we first did that, we quickly became overrun by the soul slurpers, and our tank died. After rez and rebuff, we ended up just treating this as a 'kill task'. There appeared to be no need to trap the soul slurpers, just set up somewhere safe, pull them to the group, and kill. Updates came after each kill with no use of the trap.\" - asru\n_If You Get This Step: Mobs called \"a soul slurper\" spawn and start walking up the spiral ramp. Kill these mobs. Note that you can use the \"Magical Trap\" received in the previous step to spawn an aura that freezes the slurpers in place (up to 40 seconds)._\n=====================\nKill Brutallion to prevent it from completely destroying the village 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: \"Brutallion\" spawns and starts destroying houses. Kill this mob._\n\n---\n\n**STEP #10**\nSpeak with a spiritual emissary 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Another spirit has arrived bearing a message. Speak to the spiritual emissary.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail update._\nYou say, 'Hail, a spiritual emissary'\na spiritual emissary says 'You have vanquished but a small number of the Horde. And where did their souls flee? Back to the land from whence they came, waiting to rise again and return. When the Brother comes, there will be no defeat. You will be the ones returning with us.'\n\n---\n\n**STEP #11**\nSpeak with Brother Estle 0/1 (Ethernere Tainted West Karana)\n_Task Window Says:_ Talk to Brother Estle about all that has transpired.\n_If You Get This Step: Speak with Brother Estle to complete the task._\nYou say, 'Hail, Brother Estle'\nBrother Estle says 'Thank you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. The villagers are safe, if shaken. The spirit again mentioned the 'Brother?' This is troubling. Now that we are out of immediate danger, we must hasten to find Brother Chintle. He may know more about this than I would hope. You should [leave] and rest after such hard work. Return to me soon, and we will begin the search.'\nYou have successfully helped Brother Estle fend off the Horde attack and restore order to the village. Now he will need help searching for Brother Chintle.\n\n---\n\n**TASK REWARDS**\n\\- a varying amount of platinum\n\\- a varying amount of experience\n\\- a varying number of Marks of Valor (currency used to buy group gear)\n- Mark of Valor [item=113459]\n- Spiritist's Ornate Aegis [item=114725]\n- Splinter of Potency [item=114620]",
